xnu 0202: a boot that dies at the first submission says where

One boot with gpudump=1 ends at `uc pre 71 at 0x5c7` with no `uc big 71` line
and not one further flush from any other thread: the CPU hung in the window
between that line and the fence wait. That window holds the GMU keepalive
write, the ring flush, the SMMU fault clear and the doorbell, and none of them
logs and none of them is a GPU register read the log can survive.

Print three markers that only touch memory and the log ring -- `uc keepalive
written` after the keepalive write, `uc fsr cleared` after the fault clear, `uc
ring door 0x..` before the doorbell -- so the last line in the ring names the
step that did not return: the mem flush, the GMU, the SMMU write or the
doorbell itself. They are printed for the logged submissions only, never for
the bring-up canaries.

The hang dump also gains `uc rbbm 0x.. status1 0x..`. An idle RBBM with an
unanswered fence and a clean CP is a different fault from a busy one, and that
distinction has not been available in any dump so far.
--- a/bsd/dev/mondrian_gpu.c
